തെങ്ങിൻതൈ — The Coconut Sapling
A shadow-puppet reel, made entirely in code.

Story
  The coconut-sapling tale is a version of a widely told folk parable (an elder planting a tree whose fruit they will not live to eat); public-domain folklore. Script and Malayalam dialogue written for this film.

Picture
  Puppets, scenery, carving patterns, title plaque and staging: original, generated by code (Canvas 2D + WebGL2).
  Traditional motifs (kasavu border, lattice, scale and coin patterns, meander, flame tongues) are used generically; no historical puppet or performance is copied.

Voices
  Microsoft Azure neural text-to-speech via edge-tts (https://github.com/rany2/edge-tts, LGPL-3.0 / GPL-3.0 library):
  ml-IN-SobhanaNeural (Ammumma, Appu as a boy, Minnu) and ml-IN-MidhunNeural (narrator, Appu as an old man), pitch and rate adjusted per character.
  The voices are Microsoft's online service: check Microsoft's terms yourself before using this film commercially.
  Speech check: faster-whisper (MIT) with OpenAI Whisper models (MIT); transliteration: indic-transliteration (MIT).

Music and sound
  Original score and all sound effects synthesised in mix.py (numpy/scipy); no samples or recordings.
  Mastering: pyloudnorm (MIT).

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/)
  Noto Serif Malayalam — Google / Noto project
  Cormorant Garamond — Christian Thalmann

Code
  carve.js (hide-carving toolkit) and gl.js (lamp × hide × cloth compositor) copied unchanged from Lemo-Opuscar by Lemomo (LemoLab),
  https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT License (notice in LICENSE-lemo-opuscar-MIT.txt). Rendered with that library's core/ tools.

